---
import ContentPage from '../layouts/ContentPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import { longDate } from '../lib/dates';

const effective = longDate(SITE.legalEffective);
const mail = `mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`;
---

<ContentPage
  title="Privacy policy"
  seoTitle="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.brand} handles data: calculations run in your browser and are not stored. Details on server logs, analytics, advertising cookies and your choices.`}
  lede={`Effective ${effective}. This policy explains what data ${SITE.brand} (${SITE.siteUrl}) collects, why, and the choices you have.`}
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.brand} is owned and operated by {SITE.owner}. You can reach us at
    {' '}<a href={mail}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Calculator inputs stay in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    The calculators run in your web browser. The measurements you enter are processed on your device and are not sent
    to or stored on our server. When you use <b>Share link</b>, your inputs are written into the page address (URL)
    only, so anyone you send the link to can see them.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you tick items on a materials list, the ticks are saved in your own browser (local storage) so they are still
    there when you come back. They never leave your device, and clearing your browser data removes them.
  </p>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>
    Our website is hosted by {SITE.hosting}. Like most hosts, {SITE.hosting} keeps server logs for security and
    reliability. These logs record your IP address, browser type, the pages requested and the time of each request.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics 4 to understand how visitors use the site, for example which pages are visited and how
    people arrive. Google Analytics measures visits using cookies or similar technologies. You can read
    {' '}<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from
    sites that use its services</a>, and you can opt out with the
    {' '}<a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
  <p>The site shows ads served by Google AdSense.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user’s prior visits to this website or
      other websites.
    </li>
    <li>
      Google’s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to users based on their visits to
      this site and/or other sites on the internet.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can opt out of personalised advertising in <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com" rel="noopener">My Ad
      Center</a>, and opt out of some third-party vendors’ use of cookies for personalised advertising at
      {' '}<a href="https://www.aboutads.info" rel="noopener">www.aboutads.info</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Consent (EEA, UK and Switzerland)</h2>
  <p>
    Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland see Google’s consent message (Google
    AdSense Privacy &amp; messaging, a Google-certified consent message) before personalised ads or related cookies are
    used. You can change your choice at any time with the <b>Privacy and cookie settings</b> link in the footer of every
    page.
  </p>

  <h2>If you email us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us, we use your email address and message only to reply to you. We do not add you to a mailing list or
    share your address.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This website is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from them.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to ask what personal data we hold about you, to have it
    corrected or deleted, and to object to its use. To make a request, email
    {' '}<a href={mail}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. For data held by Google (analytics and advertising), you can also use your
    Google account settings and the links above.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy, we will publish the new version on this page and update the effective date at the top.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><a href={mail}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a></p>
</ContentPage>
